From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 19:45:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] sync: add degradable query pressure protocol

Add an optional connection-level degradable root-query class and lifecycle-version capability. Preserve the legacy Connect and pressure shapes when omitted, validate all bounded lifecycle fields strictly, and serialize both declarations on reconnect.

Track active, updated, and cleared pressure epochs after applying each transition. Expose one locally deduplicated retry request for the current epoch through the base, browser, and React clients while keeping successful subscriptions, mutations, and actions unchanged.

Cover strict protocol parsing, transition and chunk ordering, reconnects, epoch replacement and clearing, retry acceptance and rejection, callback isolation, and continued non-query operation. Backend admission and application stale-state presentation remain explicit companion patches.
